":"District of Louisiana renamed Louisiana Territory and detached from Indiana Territory; the territory included all of present Missouri.","cite":"(U.S. Stat., vol. 2, ch. 31[1805]/pp. 331-332)"}},{"type":"MultiPolygon","arcs":[[[1212]],[[1213]],[[1214]],[[1215]],[[1216]],[[1217]],[[1218]],[[1219]],[[1220]],[[1221]],[[1222]],[[1223]],[[1224]],[[1225]],[[1226]],[[1227]],[[1228]],[[1229]],[[1230]],[[1231]],[[1232]],[[1233]],[[1234]],[[1235]],[[1236,1237,1238,1239,1240,1241,1242,1243,1244,1245,1246,1247,1248,-414,-413,-412,1249,1250,1251,1252,1253,1254,1255,1256]],[[1257]],[[1258]],[[1259]],[[1260]],[[1261]],[[1262]],[[1263]],[[1264]],[[1265]],[[1266]],[[1267]],[[1268]],[[1269]],[[1270,1271]]],"properties":{"id":"ma_state","v":1,"name":"Massachusetts","full":"Massachusetts","abbr":"MA","type":"State","s":17830903,"e":18041230,"power":"us","change":"Massachusetts, including the area of Maine, became an independent state on 4 July 1776. The map depicts state boundaries as of 3 September 1783.","cite":"(Declaration of Independence)"}},{"type":"MultiPolygon","arcs":[[[1212]],[[1213]],[[1214]],[[1215]],[[1216]],[[1217]],[[1218]],[[1219]],[[1220]],[[1221]],[[1222]],[[1223]],[[1224]],[[1225]],[[1226]],[[1227]],[[1228]],[[1229]],[[1230]],[[1231]],[[1232]],[[1233]],[[1234]],[[1235]],[[1236,1237,1238,1239,1240,1241,1242,1243,1244,1245,1246,1247,1248,-414,-431,-412,1249,1250,1251,1252,1253,1254,1255,1256]],[[1257]],[[1258]],[[1259]],[[1260]],[[1261]],[[1262]],[[1263]],[[1264]],[[1265]],[[1266]],[[1267]],[[1268]],[[1269]],[[1270,1271]]],"properties":{"id":"ma_state","v":2,"name":"Massachusetts","full":"Massachusetts","abbr":"MA","type":"State","s":18041231,"e":18200314,"power":"us","change":"Massachusetts gained part of the town of Southwick (the \"Southwick Jog\") that lay south of the Connecticut boundary and that had been annexed from Massachusetts in 1774.","cite":"(Hooker, 25-26; Van Zandt, 69)"}},{"type":"MultiPolygon","arcs":[[[1212]],[[1213]],[[1214]],[[1215]],[[1216]],[[1