 ch. 379/pp. 4-6; Ullman, 83-84; Van Zandt, 68)"}},{"type":"MultiPolygon","arcs":[[[1276]],[[1277]],[[1278]],[[1279]],[[1280,1281]],[[1282]],[[1283]],[[-437,1284]],[[1285,-443]],[[1286]],[[1287]],[[1288]],[[1289,1290]],[[1291]],[[1292]],[[1293]],[[1294,1295,1296,-432,434,1297,1298,1299,1300,1301,-439,1302,1303,1304]]],"properties":{"id":"md_state","v":1,"name":"Maryland","full":"Maryland","abbr":"MD","type":"State","s":17830903,"e":17910329,"power":"us","change":"Maryland became an independent state on 4 July 1776. The map depicts state boundaries as of 3 September 1783.","cite":"(Declaration of Independence)"}},{"type":"MultiPolygon","arcs":[[[1276]],[[1277]],[[1278]],[[1279]],[[1280,1281]],[[1282]],[[1283]],[[-437,1284]],[[1285,-443]],[[1286]],[[1287]],[[1288]],[[1289,1290]],[[1291]],[[1292]],[[1293]],[[1294,1295,1296,-432,-434,1297,1298,1299,1300,1301,-439,1302,1303,1304]]],"properties":{"id":"md_state","v":2,"name":"Maryland","full":"Maryland","abbr":"MD","type":"State","s":17910330,"e":99991231,"power":"us","change":"The United States created an unnamed district from land ceded by Maryland and Virginia to be the seat of national government.","cite":"(Richardson, 1:102; Van Zandt, 90)"}},{"type":"MultiPolygon","arcs":[[[1257]],[[1258]],[[1259]],[[1260]],[[1261]],[[1262]],[[1263]],[[1264]],[[1265]],[[1266]],[[1267]],[[1268]],[[1269]],[[1270,1271]]],"properties":{"id":"me_state","v":1,"name":"Maine","full":"Maine","abbr":"ME","type":"State","s":18200315,"e":99991231,"power":"us","change":"Maine was separated from Massachusetts and admitted to the Union.","cite":"(U.S. Stat., vol. 3, ch. 19 [1820]/p. 544)"}},{"type":"MultiPolygon","arcs":[[[1305,935]],[[1306,933]],[[902]],[[903]],[[904]],[[905]],[[906]],[[907]],[[908]],[[909]],[[910]],[[911]],[[912]],[[913]],[[914]],[[915]],[[916]],[[917]],[[918]],[[919]],[[855]],[[920]],[[856]],[[921]],[[862]],[[863]],[[864]],[[865]],[[866]],[[867]],[[868]],[[869]],[[870,871]],[[872,873]],[[874]],[[875]],[[876]],[[877]],[[878]],[[