 White Earth Rivers became unorganized federal territory.","cite":"(U.S. Stat., vol. 11, ch. 60[1857]/pp. 166-167 and ch. 31[1858]/p. 285; Schell, 72-77; Van Zandt, 133)"}},{"type":"MultiPolygon","arcs":[[[396,397,-958,-947,1498,-1434,961,962,963,964,965,-509,-508,966]],[[444,445,446,447,448,484,450,451,452,487,790,791,792,793,471]]],"properties":{"id":"uf_terr","v":16,"name":"Unorg. Fed. Terr.","full":"Unorganized Federal Territory","abbr":"UFT","type":"Unorganized Territory","s":18610129,"e":18610227,"power":"us","change":"Area within present Colorado that had been part of Kansas Terr. temporarily reverted to unorganized federal territory until official creation of Colorado Terr. on 28 Feb 1861. State of Kansas was admitted to the union this date; Kansas Terr. eliminated.","cite":"(U.S. Stat., vol. 12, ch. 20 [1861]/pp. 126-128; Van Zandt, 138-139)"}},{"type":"MultiPolygon","arcs":[[[-947,1498,-1434,-399,-958]],[[444,445,446,447,448,484,450,451,452,487,790,791,792,793,471]]],"properties":{"id":"uf_terr","v":17,"name":"Unorg. Fed. Terr.","full":"Unorganized Federal Territory","abbr":"UFT","type":"Unorganized Territory","s":18610228,"e":18610301,"power":"us","change":"The United States created Colorado Territory from Nebraska, New Mexico, and Utah Territories, and from the former Kansas Territory. Boundaries were identical to the state of Colorado.","cite":"(U.S. Stat., vol. 12, ch. 59[1861]/pp. 172-177; Van Zandt, 141; Noel, Mahoney, and Stevens, Historical Atlas of Colorado, ch. 2, sec. 12)"}},{"type":"Polygon","arcs":[[-947,1498,-1434,-399,-958]],"properties":{"id":"uf_terr","v":18,"name":"Unorg. Fed. Terr.","full":"Unorganized Federal Territory","abbr":"UFT","type":"Unorganized Territory","s":18610302,"e":18900501,"power":"us","change":"The United States created Dakota Territory from Nebraska Territory and Unorganized Federal Territory.","cite":"(Dak. Terr. Laws 1862, 1st sess., pp. 21-28; U.S. Stat., vol. 12, ch. 86[1861]/pp. 239-244; Van Zandt, 134, 136-137)"}},{"type":"Polygon","arcs":[[2132,-477,-405,-361,-1440,-1439,-800,-799]],"properties":{"id":"ut_state","v":1,"name":"Utah","full":"Utah","abbr":"UT","type":"State","s":18960104,"e":99991231,"power":"us","change":"The state of Utah was created from Utah Territory; Utah Territory eliminated.","cite":"(U.S. Stat., vol. 28, ch. 138 [1894]/pp. 107-112; U.S. Stat., vol. 29, procl. no. 9, [1896]/pp. 876-877; Van Zandt, 159)"}},{"type":"Polygon","arcs":[[-800,-799,-810,1334,503,504,505,506,507,508,509,510,401,402,403,-361,-365,-364,-363,-391,1332,1333,-803,-802,-801]],"properties":{"id":"ut_terr","v":1,"name":"Utah Territory","full":"Utah Territory","abbr":"UT Terr","type":"Territory","s":18500909,"e":18610227,"power":"us","change":"The United States created Utah Territory from the territory ceded by Mexico in the Treaty of Guadalupe-Hidalgo (1848), from territory to be purchased from the state of Texas in December 1850, and from unorganized federal territory.","cite":"(U.S. Stat., vol. 9, ch. 49[1850]/pp. 446-452 and ch. 51[1850]/pp. 453-458; Van Zandt, 159)"}},{"type":"Polygon","arcs":[[-800,-799,-810,1334,503,504,-407,-406,-405,-361,-365,-364,-363,-391,1332,1333,-803,-802,-801]],"properties":{"id":"ut_terr","v":2,"name":"Utah Territory","full":"Utah Territory","abbr":"UT Terr","type":"Territory","s":18610228,"e":18610301,"power":"us","change":"The United States created Colorado Territory from Nebraska, New Mexico, and Utah Territories, and from the former Kansas Territory.","cite":"(U.S. Stat., vol. 12, ch. 59[1861]/pp. 172-177; Van Zandt, 141)"}},{"type":"Polygon","arcs":[[-800,-799,-810,-478,-477,-405,-361,-365,-364,-1446,-1445,-1444,-1443,-1442,-1441,-802,-801]],"properties":{"id":"ut_terr","v":3,"name":"Utah Territory","full":"Utah Territory","abbr":"UT Terr","type":"Territory","s":18610302,"e":18620713,"power":"us","change":"The United States created Nevada Territory from Utah Territory. Utah Territory also lost to Nebraska Territory when Nebraska Territory gained area in present Wyoming from Utah Territory.","cite":"(U.S. Stat., vol. 12, ch. 83[1861], pp. 209-210 and ch. 86[1861], pp. 239-244; Van Zandt, 134, 136-137, 158-160)"}},{"type":"Polygon","arcs":[[-800,-799,-810,-478,-477,-405,-361,-365,-1438,-1437,-801]],"properties":{"id":"ut_terr","v":4,"name":"Utah Territory","full":"Utah Territory","abbr":"UT Terr","type":"Territory","s":18620714,"e":18660504,"power":"us","change":"Nevada Territory gained from Utah Territory.","cite":"(U.S. Stat., vol. 12, ch. 173 [1862], p. 575; Van Zandt, 158-160)"}},{"type":"Polygon","arcs":[[-478,-477,-405,-361,-1440,-1439,-800,-799,-810]],"properties":{"id":"ut_terr","v":5,"name":"Utah Territory","full":"Utah Territory","abbr":"UT Terr","type":"Territory","s":18660505,"e":18680724,"power":"us","change":"The state of Nevada gained from Utah Territory.","cite":"(U.S. Stat., vol. 14, ch. 73[1866]/p. 43; Van Zandt, 158-159)"}},{"type":"Polygon","arcs":[[2132,-477,-405,-361,-1440,-1439,-800,-799]],"properties":{"id":"ut_terr","v":6,"name":"Utah Territory","full":"Utah Territory","abbr":"UT Terr","type":"Territory","s":18680725,"e":18960103,"power":"us","change":"The United States created Wyoming Territory from Dakota, Idaho, and Utah Territories.","cite":"(U.S. Stat., vol. 15, ch. 235[1868], secs. 1, 17/pp. 178, 183; Van Zandt, 136, 144)"}},{"type":"MultiPolygon","arcs":[[[-1392,2133]],[[967,968]],[[2134]],[[2135]],[[2136]],[[2137]],[[2138]],[[2139]],[[2140]],[[2141]],[[2142]],[[2143]],[[2144]],[[-1304,2145]],[[2146,-1281]],[[416]],[[419]],[[420]],[[421]],[[422]],[[423]],[[424]],[[902]],[[903]],[[904]],[[905]],[[906]],[[907]],[[908]],[[909]],[[910]],[[911]],[[912]],[[913]],[[914]],[[915]],[[916]],[[917]],[[918]],[[919]],[[855]],[[920]],[[856]],[[921]],[[857]],[[858]],[[859]],[[860]],[[861]],[[862]],[[863]],[[864]],[[865]],[[866]],[[867]],[[868]],[[869]],[[870,871]],[[872,873]],[[874]],[[875]],[[876]],[[877]],[[878]],[[879]],[[880]],[[881]],[[882]],[[883]],[[922]],[[884]],[[885]],[[923]],[[924]],